{
  "assessment": "The source supports the normalized-friction fits for the viscous-inertial transition. The public control St ranges from 0.01 to 300. The common fixed condition K_phi = J + 0.1 I^2 = 0.065 is supported by the two simulation runs at St=0.65 and 206.5. The derived relations J(St)=0.065/(1+0.1 St), K_mu(St)=0.065*(1+alpha_mu St)/(1+0.1 St), and r(St)=1+a_mu*sqrt(K_mu(St)) are consistent with the source equations and fits. The private branch mu_f=0.15 uses a_mu=14.3 and alpha_mu=0.029; the alternate branch mu_f=0.80 uses a_mu=26.5 and alpha_mu=0.00875. All constants are anchored. The case is authoring-ready.",
  "case_authoring_ready": true,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Sudarshan Konidena, Tangential Forces Govern the Viscous-Inertial Transition in Dense Frictional Suspensions, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/66pp-4rdj",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/66pp-4rdj",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2505.04242v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "Particle-resolved simulations of dense frictional suspensions undergoing the viscous-inertial transition using pressure-imposed rheology. The study varies fluid viscosity, shear rate, and granular pressure, and examines the effect of interparticle friction on the transition. The key findings are the distinct scalings of packing fraction phi and macroscopic friction mu, governed by different alpha values, and the role of tangential contact and lubrication forces.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "viscous_inertial_rheology",
      "statement": "The macroscopic friction coefficient mu is governed by a single dimensionless number K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2, with alpha_mu = 1/St_{v->i}^mu, and the normalized friction r = mu/mu_c follows r = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu). The packing fraction phi follows phi = phi_c (1 - a_phi sqrt(K_phi)) with K_phi = J + alpha_phi I^2 and alpha_phi = 0.1.",
      "equations": [
        "K_phi = J + alpha_phi I^2, alpha_phi = 0.1",
        "K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2",
        "r = mu/mu_c = 1 + a_mu * sqrt(K_mu)",
        "phi = phi_c (1 - a_phi sqrt(K_phi))"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["St", "J", "I", "K_phi", "K_mu", "mu", "mu_c", "r", "a_mu", "alpha_mu", "phi", "phi_c", "a_phi", "alpha_phi"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "alpha_phi",
          "value": 0.1,
          "uncertainty": "none reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "coefficient in K_phi definition",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 246, "line_end": 246, "support": "K=K_phi=J+alpha_phi I^2, where alpha_phi=1/St_{v->i}=0.1"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a_mu_muf015",
          "value": 14.3,
          "uncertainty": "none reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "fit coefficient in r = 1 + a_mu sqrt(K_mu) for mu_f=0.15",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 177, "line_end": 177, "support": "inset provides mu/mu_c vs K_mu with a single fit mu = mu_c (1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) with a_mu=14.3"},
            {"line_start": 358, "line_end": 358, "support": "Table: mu_f=0.15, a_mu=14.3"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "alpha_mu_muf015",
          "value": 0.029,
          "uncertainty": "none reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "coefficient in K_mu for mu_f=0.15",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 252, "line_end": 252, "support": "K_mu = J + alpha_mu I^2 with alpha_mu = 0.029"},
            {"line_start": 358, "line_end": 358, "support": "Table: mu_f=0.15, alpha_mu=0.029"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "a_mu_muf080",
          "value": 26.5,
          "uncertainty": "none reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "fit coefficient in r = 1 + a_mu sqrt(K_mu) for mu_f=0.80",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 360, "line_end": 360, "support": "Table: mu_f=0.80, a_mu=26.5"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "alpha_mu_muf080",
          "value": 0.00875,
          "uncertainty": "none reported",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "coefficient in K_mu for mu_f=0.80",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 360, "line_end": 360, "support": "Table: mu_f=0.80, alpha_mu=0.00875"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "mu_c",
          "value": 0.3,
          "uncertainty": "±0.02 for mu_f=0.15, ±0.05 for mu_f=0.5, ±0.08 for mu_f=0.8",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "critical macroscopic friction at jamming",
          "anchors": [
            {"line_start": 248, "line_end": 248, "support": "mu_c = 0.30 ± 0.02 at jamming"},
            {"line_start": 358, "line_end": 360, "support": "Table: mu_c values for different mu_f"}
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {"line_start": 123, "line_end": 123, "support": "K = J + alpha I^2 with alpha = 1/St_{v->i}"},
        {"line_start": 177, "line_end": 177, "support": "Fits mu = mu_c(1 + a_mu K_mu^{1/2}) with a_mu=14.3"},
        {"line_start": 246, "line_end": 252, "support": "Definitions of K_phi and K_mu with alpha_phi=0.1 and alpha_mu=0.029"},
        {"line_start": 358, "line_end": 360, "support": "Table of fit coefficients for mu_f=0.15, 0.5, 0.8"}
      ]
    }
  ],
